== Catalan numbers are not moments of a bounded measure on Z_p:
   k=(p^m-1)/2 gives C_k a unit, k'=k+(p-1)p^(h-1), h=m-1, gives p | C_k', although
   x^(k+phi(p^h)) = x^k mod p^h on Z_p, for k>=h
   p=3 m=3: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=3 m=4: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=3 m=5: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=5 m=3: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=5 m=4: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=5 m=5: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=7 m=3: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=7 m=4: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=7 m=5: v_p(C_k)=0 v_p(C_k')=1
   p=2 m=4: k=2^m-1, k'=k+2^(m-1): v_2(C_k)=0 v_2(C_k')=1
   p=2 m=6: k=2^m-1, k'=k+2^(m-1): v_2(C_k)=0 v_2(C_k')=1
   p=2 m=8: k=2^m-1, k'=k+2^(m-1): v_2(C_k)=0 v_2(C_k')=1
